## Things I was unsure of / did not verify
- **An out-of-repo write happened and was undone.** My first `_venv_root` red-check made the fake create `<real Application Support>/OhYesMLX/engines/mlxlm-0.31.3/bin` (empty), because `_relocate` depends on `_venv_root`. I removed it with `rmdir` (empty-only); the real `optiq-0.5.13` venv, `lab-paths.json` (Oct 30 mtime), `install-log.jsonl` (Oct 30) and `fetched.json` (Nov 3) were not written. I then made `do_install` pin `DEFAULT_ENV.home` to `tmp_path` so no install test can leave the scratch tree even when the code under test breaks, and gave `FakeRun` the one real side effect of `-m venv` (`<root>/bin`).
- No pip install, runtime, or live install was run; the hashes are PyPI's own metadata, not independently `curl`+`shasum`-checked (that is the plan's Task 2 step).
- `hash_freeze.py` joins `\` continuations with its own 10-line helper, and `engines._check_hashed_requirements` has another; putting it in `__init__.py` was outside "add `atomic_write_text` only".
- Names I chose (not specified): `_check_hashed_requirements`, `_HASHED_PIN`, `_PIN_ONLY`, `_requirement_lines`, `_require_pypi`; `main` treats `argv` as `sys.argv[1:]`.
- The late threshold is strict `>` 7 days (exactly 7 is not late — tested). Extra read-only metadata fetches for numpy/pygame/tokenizers confirmed real upload spans are 0 days, so empty `LATE UPLOADS` is plausible.

